Changelog: 24-11-2026 17:44:44

Release 0.13.2.

Changelog: 24-11-2026 15:16:11

Fixed. The hints that name which program logged the unexplained warnings were lost when the journal writes the month
in another language, such as "nov 24" in Dutch. Any month name now counts.

Fixed. Test 32 missed a staged deployment when rpm-ostree ran outside a UTF-8 locale, as under LC_ALL=C. rpm-ostree
then marks the booted deployment with * instead of the bullet, so the test said the booted one was the newest. It now
reads both marks.

Fixed. Test 33 reported an available update whenever the check printed anything other than "No updates available",
for example offline or while another rpm-ostree job ran. It now reads rpm-ostree's exit code. A check that did not
finish says so, and says nothing about updates.

Fixed. On a flattened image, a dnf update check that failed or timed out said that no updates were found. It now
reads dnf's exit code, and a check that did not finish says so.

Fixed. Test 37 read the VRAM split from card1 first and then from the last card that reports VRAM, so a second GPU
took the board's place. It now reads the board's GPU, the one the script finds at its start.

Changelog: 24-11-2026 13:15:49

Release 0.13.1.

Changelog: 24-11-2026 13:11:31

Fixed. Test 36 never found a kernel Oops line by the word Oops. Its pattern \bOops\b went to awk with -v, which
turns \b into a backspace, so the word never matched under gawk either. An Oops was only caught through its Call
Trace line. The pattern now marks the word with characters both awk and grep -E read the same, and Whoopsie still
doesn't match. tests/test_awk.py checks it under gawk, mawk and grep -E.

Changelog: 24-11-2026 13:06:54

Fixed. test-board.sh's awk programs now give the same results under mawk, the awk of Debian and Ubuntu, as under
gawk, the awk of Bazzite. On Bazzite nothing changes. The zram check prints the zram size and the total memory with
printf, because mawk's print writes 16 GiB as 1.7e+10 and bash can't count with that. The kernel fault scan ignores
case through tolower(), because mawk ignores IGNORECASE. The MangoHud analysis sorts the frame times with its own heap
sort, because mawk has no asort() and stops there. A new test, tests/test_awk.py, runs these programs under gawk and
mawk where they are installed.

Changelog: 24-11-2026 12:37:14

Fixed. PS5 CPU Tools is now called PS5 Core Unlock in the comments and messages of
development/tools/install-requirements.sh.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 21:58:21

Release 0.13.0.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 20:00:16

Release 0.12.0.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 18:11:59

Added. Help is a readable page now. The chapter's text stands in a column of about 90 characters, in larger type with
room between the lines, under the app's icon instead of the large picture. Its sections are listed on the left, and a
click jumps to one. Find in the help searches the page. Back and Wiki are pills: Wiki opens the page in the browser, and
Open in editor is gone. The chapter says so, and tests/test_smoke.py checks it.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 18:05:41

Fixed. The app's chapter was checked against the code, and its texts with it. Test 15 reads the current boot's journal
errors, not only the kernel's, and test 16 reads warnings and errors. Test 31 lists /var/log and checks that it exists,
and does not check that it is writable. Test 18 warns when a governor for other hardware is active or enabled. The
Settings page said that Older than N days also removes the runs' history entries: their results stay in the history. The
chapter now says that only a report's result lines carry a tag, and names the Steam Machine among the GPU comparison's
systems.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 16:58:55

Fixed. The Finished box's tooltip said it counts the tests with a result in this session. It counts the latest result of
each test over all runs, and the tooltip says so now.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 12:25:09

Release 0.11.0.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 20:53:56

Release 0.10.0.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 19:53:10

Added. Test 19 compares the clock amdgpu reads from the GPU with the one ps5-gpufreq asked for. When the GPU runs
more than 100 MHz above it at idle, the test warns and its hint gives two min_freq writes that bring the clock down.
After a wake or a boot the GPU can stay at a high clock this way, at about 70 W more at the wall.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 12:04:43

Release 0.9.0.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 19:26:09

Release 0.8.0.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 15:16:09

Release 0.7.0.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 14:57:33

Added. Test 60, VKCube, on the Performance page: it draws the Vulkan tools' spinning cube in a window for five
seconds, as the desktop user in the running session, and passes when vkcube is still drawing after that time. It is
an error when vkcube ended by itself, with its output. Without a graphical session or without vkcube it is skipped.
It runs with Run all and by itself (--only=60). Test 41 starts vkcube only when no other GPU load tool is
installed, so the cube was never seen on a console that has them.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 14:57:33

Added. development/tools/install-requirements.sh installs Prime95's mprime with --mprime, and with --all: the
release mersenne.org's download page lists at that moment, compared with the SHA-256 listed there, unpacked into
~/mprime with a link in ~/.local/bin. A run with a newer release on the page installs that one over it;
~/mprime/.release names the release that is there. When the page cannot be read, it installs the one release the
script knows (30.19 build 20). No test uses mprime: PS5 CPU Tools runs its torture test for a longer burn-in, and
looks in ~/mprime first.

